{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nGerrit rejects a valid review upload from a clean worktree with `remote unpack failed: error Missing tree 1959f268184dce88f62132173dfbf24e823ceb89`. The failure blocks comment-remediation changes from entering review and appears to be Gerrit repository/object-store health, not the patch.\n\n## Evidence\n- Worktree: `/Users/joeoakhart/comment-remediation-47be`.\n- Commit: `be29a0057028f539a34f79658fb57f09d40f0422`; parent and current `origin/main`: `710a606b6d38bafc0f2c6684711b08811d26529e`.\n- Normal upload `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` was rejected before a change was created.\n- A second upload with `git push --no-thin gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` failed with the identical missing-tree object.\n- Locally, `git cat-file -t 1959f268184dce88f62132173dfbf24e823ceb89` returns `tree`, and the leaf revision walk reports no missing objects.\n- No server-side repair or further retry was attempted in the comment/documentation session.\n\n## Investigation plan\n- Reproduce against the Gerrit repository and inspect the receive-pack/JGit logs for the rejected upload.\n- Verify Gerrit's `main` ref, reachable object graph, alternates/promisor configuration, recent replication, and repository consistency around the named tree.\n- Determine why a non-thin pack still leaves the server resolving the tree as missing.\n- Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path, then verify ordinary review upload and receive-pack health.\n- Document the root cause, blast radius, safe recovery, and recurrence prevention.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The missing-tree rejection is reproduced or conclusively tied to retained server logs.\n- [x] The precise Gerrit repository/object-store root cause is proven with concrete evidence.\n- [x] Repository integrity is restored through a backed-up, supported recovery procedure.\n- [x] A normal `HEAD:refs/for/main` review upload succeeds without `--no-thin`.\n- [x] Existing refs/changes and `main` remain valid and no review data is lost.\n- [x] Recovery and prevention evidence are recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788834072902867001,"uuid":"ac13a4d7-45e8-47f3-87c6-febda60cc703"}